          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Suppose we have a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibered+category"} fibered category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℬ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \colon \mathcal{E} \to \mathcal{B}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories+with+families"} type families
            (living in the fibers of
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contexts"} contexts
            (living in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℬ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics+of+dependent+types"} categorical semantics of dependent types
          %p
            A
            %strong definable collection
            of objects of the total category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            corresponds, intuitively, to the extension of a ‘meta-property’ of the types which we can use to single out subcontexts by means of a generalized ‘
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comprehension+category"}> comprehension
            ’.
          %p#ArchetypicalExample
            The archetypal example is given by ‘
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truth"}> truth
            ’: Suppose
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            has
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibred+terminal+objects"} fibred terminal objects
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/context"} context
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi ℬ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B \colon \mathcal{B}
            = succeed "\u2019" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+type"} unit type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msub
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1_B \colon \mathcal{E}_B
            which is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal
            in the fiber. Then the collection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msub
                    %mn 1
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{1_B \colon \mathcal{E} \mid B \colon \mathcal{B}\}
            is an extensive definition of the meta-property of ‘being true’ (or better: being
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+type"} inhabited
          %p
            Once we have a definable collection
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒫
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X: \mathcal{E}_B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            ‘satisfy’
            = succeed "?" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi b
                    %mo :
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi b
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝒫
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ↣
                    %mi B
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℬ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{b:B \mid X_b : \mathcal{P}\} \rightarrowtail B : \mathcal{B}
          %p
            In a sense, a definable collection is a very weak notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreflective+subcategory"} coreflective subfibration
            (i.e. a fibred coreflective subcategory).
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            We follow the exposition in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Jacobs"} (Jacobs ‘99)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+fibration"} fibration
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℬ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p:\mathcal{E} \to \mathcal{B}
          %h3#of_collections_of_objects Of collections of objects
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒫
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}
              be a collection of object in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℰ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒫
                      %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}_B
              the subcollection of those objects in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒫
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}
              over a chosen
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℬ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B:\mathcal{B}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  We say
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒫
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}
                  is
                  %strong closed under substitution
                  if for each map
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi u
                        %mo :
                        %mi J
                        %mo →
                        %mi I
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u:J \to I
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℬ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}
                  and
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi P
                          %mo :
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝒫
                            %mi I
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P : \mathcal{P}_I
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi u
                            %mo *
                          %mi P
                          %mo :
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝒫
                            %mi J
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} u^*P : \mathcal{P}_J
              %li
                %p
                  We say
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒫
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}
                  is
                  %strong definable
                  if it is closed under substitution and, for each object
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo :
                          %mi ℰ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X: \mathcal{E}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi X
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mi 𝒫
                        %mo :
                        %mi 𝒫
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{X\}_{\mathcal{P}} : \mathcal{P}
                  and a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+morphism"} cartesian morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mi X
                        %mo :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi X
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mi 𝒫
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i_X : \{X\}_{\mathcal{P}} \to X
                  which is universal among cartesian morphisms into
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                  from an object in
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒫
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}
            %p
          %p
            The constructor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mi 𝒫
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{-\}_{\mathcal{P}}
            is the generalized comprehension we were mentioning above. Indeed, we have the following characterization:
          %p
          .num_lemma
            %h6 Lemma
            %p
              %em
                (Lemma 9.6.2 in
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "#Jacobs"} (Jacobs ‘99)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒫
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}
              be a collection closed under substitution. Then the following our equivalent:
            %ol
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒫
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{P}
                is definable
              %li
                For each object
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi ℰ
                        %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X: \mathcal{E}_B
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℬ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}
                defined as
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                        %mo ↦
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mi u
                        %mo :
                        %mi J
                        %mo →
                        %mi I
                        %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∣
                        %msup
                          %mi u
                          %mo *
                        %mi X
                        %mo :
                        %mi 𝒫
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        J \mapsto \{u : J \to I \mid u^*X : \mathcal{P}\}
                %p is representable.
            %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p
              The idea is that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{X\}_P
              is the representing object for the presheaf object of (2).
          %h3#of_collections_of_functors Of collections of functors
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              be a category, that we think of as trivially fibred
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo !
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %mo :
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo →
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} !_{\mathcal{C}} : \mathcal{C} \to 1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mo !
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %mo →
                    %mi p
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo :
                        %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{(I_a, f_a) : !_{\mathcal{C}} \to p\}_{a:A}
              (where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is a
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
              %span.newWikiWord
                exponent fibration
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/exponent+fibration"} ?
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi p
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo !
                            %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^{!_{\mathcal{C}}}
          %p
            Recall the exponent fibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi p
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo !
                        %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p^{!_{\mathcal{C}}}
            is a fibration over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℬ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}
            whose fiber over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo :
                  %mi ℬ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I:\mathcal{B}
            is given by functors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C} \to \mathcal{E}_I
            and whose reindexing is given by post-composition with the reindexing functors of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %span.newWikiWord
              exponent fibration
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/exponent+fibration"} ?
            for more details.
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              Clearly this definition generalizes the previous one since collections of objects of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              are given by collections of functors out of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
          %h3#of_collections_of_vertical_morphisms Of collections of vertical morphisms
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A collection of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertical+morphisms"} vertical morphisms
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
              is definable iff it is definable as collection of functors out of the arrow category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \downarrow
          %h3#of_subfibrations Of subfibrations
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %span.newWikiWord
                subfibration
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/subfibration"} ?
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ′
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mo ′
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℬ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p': \mathcal{E}' \to \mathcal{B}
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              is definable iff its collection of objects and vertical morphisms are both definable.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              has a fibred terminal objects, then their collection is definable if and only if the functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℬ
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℰ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1: \mathcal{B} \to \mathcal{E}
              has a right adjoint
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo :
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo →
                      %mi ℬ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{-\}:\mathcal{E} \to \mathcal{B}
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Fam
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : \mathrm{Fam}(\mathcal{C}) \to \mathbf{Set}
              a fibration of families (a family over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi I
                    %mo :
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I:\mathbf{Set}
              is a n
              = succeed "-indexed" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              (Lemma 9.6.4 in in
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#Jacobs"} (Jacobs ‘99)
          %h2#see_also See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibred+category"} fibred category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comprehension+category"} comprehension category
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+comprehension"} axiom of comprehension
          %h2#references References
          %p Definability is introduced on p.35 (‘Short annotated glossary’) of
          %ul
            %li#Benabou85
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jean+B%C3%A9nabou"}> Jean Bénabou
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Fibered categories and the foundations of naive category theory
              = succeed "(1)" do
                %strong 50
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.2307/2273784"} 10.2307/2273784
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/2273784"} JSTOR
          %p A modern and more traditional account is given in Section 9.6 of
          %ul
            %li#Jacobs
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bart+Jacobs"}> Bart Jacobs
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Categorical Logic and Type Theory
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 141
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://www.sciencedirect.com/bookseries/studies-in-logic-and-the-foundations-of-mathematics/vol/141"} ISBN:978-0-444-50170-7
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://people.mpi-sws.org/~dreyer/courses/catlogic/jacobs.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.cs.ru.nl/B.Jacobs/CLT/bookinfo.html"} webpage
